Soon Mother appeared in the room, already dressed up for a trip. She took pasties, kissed her daughter and left the house.
The weather was marvelous, spring Sun was warming up the air, birds were twitting. Snow still remained somewhere in the forest, but the path was already free from the winter cover and woman slowly marched over soft but no boggy ground.
The walk was long and after a few hours on fresh air woman felt much clearer that smells of the forest were mixing with smell of still warm pasties with hunchback salmon. 